{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411149-order-of-hermes-inspiration","id":1411149,"title":"Order of Hermes: Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-30T19:34:42-07:00","id":1411149,"title":"Order of Hermes: Inspiration","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> I've had a hard time looking for hermetic-related inspiration in fiction, particularly in movies and comic books (no time for books, much less real hermetism). Any movies or comics or short fiction products I could use? I know there is at least one thread about inspiration for Mage, but I need Order of Hermes only. <br /> <br /> Thanx in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T19:47:22-07:00","id":1411153,"title":"","content":"Have you read the Tradition books for Order of Hermes? Both the original and Revised version have suggestions. So, too, does Tales of Dark Magic if you want action-movie references from a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:29:00-07:00","id":1411159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1411149-order-of-hermes-inspiration#post1411149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> I've had a hard time looking for hermetic-related inspiration in fiction, particularly in movies and comic books (no time for books, much less real hermetism). Any movies or comics or short fiction products I could use? I know there is at least one thread about inspiration for Mage, but I need Order of Hermes only.<br /> <br /> Thanx in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harry Potter seems very Order of Hermes inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T16:06:11-07:00","id":1411267,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Order_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">A Netflix show called The Order,</a> where a guy joins the Hermetic Order of the Blue Rose wasn't bad... Except the ending of the show was a let down. The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartimaeus_Sequence\" target=\"_blank\">Bartimaeus </a>books are good. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Magicians_(Grossman_novel)\" target=\"_blank\">The Magicians</a> Trilogy by Lev Grossman, I also quite liked them.<br /> <br /> Also, the Allen Moore comic series, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promethea\" target=\"_blank\">Promethea</a>, is recommended in the inspirational materials in the Revised Tradition book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 09-01-2020, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:59:38-07:00","id":1411399,"title":"","content":"I'll second Alan Moore and JH Williams's <b>Promethea</b>. Its second arc is very much a crash course in Western mystical theory, including the Tarot and the Qabalah Tree of Life. <br /> <br /> Also Moore's <b>From Hell</b> graphic novel (with Eddie Campbell), about the Jack the Ripper murders as a bizarre Masonic/Hermetic ritual to usher in a dark 20th century, goes into some detail about its assorted mystical aspects, including copious footnotes. <br /> <br /> While not entirely Hermetic in nature, if you've never seen the films <i>Lord of Illusions</i> (1995), <i>Pi</i> (1998), <i>The Ninth Gate</i> (1999), <i>The Illusionist</i> (2006), <i>The Prestige</i> (2006), <i>The Sorcerers' Apprentice</i> (2010), and <i>The Alchemist Cookbook</i> (2016), they offer some interesting ideas. <br /> <br /> As far as gaming sourcebooks, <b>Halls of the Arcanum</b> (Mage's Year of the Hunter book about the Arcanum, who practice a lot of classic Western ritual magic similar to some of the Order's Art) and <b>GURPS Cabal </b>(which involves a lot of Hermetic magic and cosmology). <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T02:09:06-07:00","id":1411621,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest the short lived &quot;Constantine&quot; tv show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T05:18:40-07:00","id":1411632,"title":"","content":"The most authentically realized magical ritual I\u2019ve seen in movies is A Dark Song, which is set in an isolated house in Wales with a woman who has lost a child and recruits an alcoholic (and generally abusive) occultist to carry out a ritual in order to commune with him. It\u2019s low key, but it presents a real hermetic ritual as it was performed by people like Crowley and others. <br /> <br /> If you want to go really academic on it, then read up on the poetry of William Blake or W.B Yeats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}